== Sauce ==

Mix @kecap manis{3%tbsp}, @fish sauce{2%tbsp}, and @white pepper{1/8%tsp} in a small bowl. Toss @chicken thighs{500%g}(boneless, skinless, cut into small bite size pieces) with 1 1/2 tbsp of the sauce, set the rest aside for drizzling.

== Mushrooms ==

Heat @oil{2 1/2%tbsp} in a #large heavy based pot{} on high heat. Cook half the @shiitake mushrooms{150%g}(fresh, small halved, large thickly sliced) with a pinch of @salt{} and @white pepper{} until some of the mushrooms have a light tinge of golden on the surface, but don't try to cook them all the way through. Remove into a bowl. Repeat with remaining mushrooms.

== Chicken ==

Heat the remaining @oil{1%tbsp} until hot. Add the chicken and stir for 1 minute, just until the surface is sealed but inside still raw. Add the white part of @green onion stems{}(finely sliced), @garlic{2%cloves}(finely minced), and @ginger{1 1/2%tbsp}(grated), stir for 30 seconds. Add @long grain rice{1 1/2%cups}(NOT RINSED), stir briefly just to coat in oil.

== Simmer ==

Add @chicken stock{2%cups}(low sodium) and @ginger{4-5%slices}(~5mm / 0.2" thick, no need to peel). Bring to a rapid simmer. Scatter mushrooms across the surface (add any pooled liquid too), then let it come to a rapid simmer again.

== Steam ==

Put the lid on, reduce stove to low (or medium low, for weak burners). Cook for ~{20%minutes} (do not stir) until the liquid is fully absorbed.

== Rest ==

Remove pot from the stove with the lid still on and rest for ~{10%minutes}.

== Drizzle and Toss ==

Drizzle remaining sauce all over, add the green part of @green onion stems{4}(cut into 5cm/2" lengths). Gently toss until the green onion is mostly wilted. Serve!
